abstract: >-
  FaDeS (Façade Debris Simulator) simulates the out-of-plane overturning of a
  masonry façade and the debris it leaves on the street. A two-dimensional
  section of the façade overturns about its outer toe, breaks into its blocks at
  the first impact, and the blocks settle on the street in the planck.js engine;
  the extent of the debris is measured as P95 by mass and Lmax, and, for a given
  street width, as the width left free. Any wall can be simulated, in total or
  partial collapse, with its own height, thickness, block size, diatone courses
  and materials, one at a time with its animation or many at a time from a grid
  or a CSV file. For walls in total collapse it also checks the rigid phase
  against a closed form, and the integrity of the falling panel with no tensile
  strength or with any tensile strength. It is the simulator of the paper
  "Simulating the debris of overturning masonry façades with rigid blocks: from
  the falling panel to the documented collapses" and reproduces its analyses,
  comparing every run of the paper's campaigns with the paper's stored results.
  Desktop application for Windows and macOS, and command line.
keywords:
  - masonry
  - façade
  - out-of-plane overturning
  - debris
  - rigid blocks
  - rigid-body contact dynamics
  - earthquake
  - street blockage
